  "body": "Found by the #926 per-post script suites (recorded stream `probe`: a bore-centre probe, rpm 0, no `PARAM Coolant` - the stream's silent default, Flood).\n\n**What is wrong.** `doosan-dnm.cps` posts `M8` (flood coolant on) in the probe section, right after `T07 M6 / G43 H07`, and `M9` at the end. The probe tests' own law (`crates/app/tests/probe_op.rs`, `probe_dialects.rs`, `probe_tormach.rs`: \"a touch probe starts no spindle and no coolant\") holds for the other posts only because those tests post machine-less: `coolantFor(\"flood\")` in `fanuc.cps` (and the posts built on it) returns the machine's Flood M-code, so on any machine file that lists a Flood coolant a probe section also gets `M8`. Doosan returns `M8` even with no machine. #523 gated the spindle for a section with no speed; coolant was not gated.\n\nWhy P1: wrong output a user hits - flood coolant during probing (wet stylus, chips and coolant on the measured surfaces); no gouge.\n\nDone means: a probing section (a section carrying TOUCH/FOUND records, or rpm 0) starts no coolant on any mill post, with or without a machine stating coolants; pinned by the #926 `probe` golden of `doosan-dnm` (listed as a known bug in `crates/post/tests/recorded/mod.rs`) and a machine-with-coolants case.\n",
